--
N5008 [temp.deduct.call] + [dcl.fct]/2 + [temp.variadic]/5 + [expr.new]:
a free function template whose trailing return type is
`decltype(::new((void*)0) _Tp(declval<_Args>()...))` (the C++20
std::construct_at declaration) must expand the `_Args` pack inside the
new-initializer of the return-type decltype during argument deduction.
Was KNOWNBUG (>= 2 args constructing a class-template instance: "found no
match for symbol 'construct_at'").  Fixed by teaching
template_mapt::expand_call_argument_packs (which apply(decltype) invokes)
to treat a cpp_new initializer's expression-list as a pack-expansion
context, mirroring the function-call argument list it already handled.
g++/clang++ runtime-verified.
